From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Opsero <support@opsero.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 18:28:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] net: axienet: default to 1024 RX descriptors on MRMAC ports

The MRMAC has no RX backpressure (its RX AXI-Stream has no tready), so
the AXI MCDMA S2MM channel behind it silently discards a whole frame
whenever the RX descriptor ring has no free descriptor. The driver's
default ring of 128 descriptors is refilled from NAPI; any scheduling
gap longer than ~128 frame times (~150 us of 1500-byte frames at 10G,
~60 us at 25G) therefore loses frames. The loss is invisible in the MAC
and netdev error counters and only shows up as TCP retransmits and as
the MCDMA S2MM packet-drop count (MCDMA base + 0x514).

Measured on VCK190 + Quad SFP28 FMC (TCP host->board, 30 s):
  10G: 50415 retransmits with 128 RX BDs, 226 with 1024
  25G: 73348 retransmits with 128 RX BDs, 3599 with 1024

Default MRMAC ports to 1024 RX descriptors. The TX ring and all other
MAC types keep their defaults; "ethtool -G" still overrides the value
while the interface is down.

Memory cost per port with a 1500-byte MTU: 1024 x ~2 KiB RX skbs plus
1024 x 128 B coherent descriptors, i.e. ~2.1 MiB instead of ~0.26 MiB,
allocated only while the interface is up.
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/xilinx/xilinx_axienet_main.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/xilinx/xilinx_axienet_main.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/xilinx/xilinx_axienet_main.c
index 6dfa4a4fbfdd..c0c4b8604f25 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/xilinx/xilinx_axienet_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/xilinx/xilinx_axienet_main.c
@@ -58,6 +58,10 @@
 
 /* Descriptors defines for Tx and Rx DMA */
 #define RX_BD_NUM_DEFAULT		128
+/* MRMAC RX has no backpressure: the MCDMA S2MM drops whole frames whenever
+ * the RX ring has no free descriptor, so give MRMAC ports a deeper ring.
+ */
+#define RX_BD_NUM_MRMAC_DEFAULT		1024
 #define TX_BD_NUM_MIN			(MAX_SKB_FRAGS + 1)
 #define TX_BD_NUM_MAX			4096
 #define RX_BD_NUM_MAX			4096
@@ -5267,6 +5271,11 @@ static int axienet_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		}
 	}
 
+	/* Still adjustable with "ethtool -G" while the interface is down */
+	if (lp->axienet_config &&
+	    lp->axienet_config->mactype == XAXIENET_MRMAC)
+		lp->rx_bd_num = RX_BD_NUM_MRMAC_DEFAULT;
+
 	/* Setup checksum offload, but default to off if not specified */
 	lp->features = 0;
 #ifndef CONFIG_AXIENET_HAS_MCDMA
-- 
